          "lines": [
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "## Steps"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "1. [P1] Read the request in your prompt: its inputs, every acceptance criterion and the deliverable. The criteria come from the contract and can only be met, never changed; copy the relevant ones verbatim into every task you delegate."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "2. [P2] Delegate to `writer` (Writer) with `budget=3`: its part of the request, with the criteria it must meet."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "3. [P3] When the work exists, delegate to `reviewer` (Independent Reviewer) with `budget=2` to check the final file independently against every criterion. It reports findings and required changes to you and never edits the author's file."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "4. [P4] If a check fails: send the required changes, quoted verbatim, to the AUTHOR of the failing file (`delegate(to=<author>, revises=<that author's task id>, budget=1)`; for the deliverable usually `writer`), then have the checker re-check that same file (`delegate(to=<checker>, revises=<the checker's task id>)`). One rework and one re-check; if it still fails, report `blocked` with options and the checker's final line instead of starting another cycle."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "5. [P5] Read the final artifact yourself and check it against EVERY criterion of the request, quoting counts from your own `read` output, and paste the checker's final coverage line verbatim."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "6. [P6] Report: `done` only if every criterion is met (else `blocked` with the deviation and a recommended decision). Name the deliverable's path (the assistant copies it to /tmp/hirearchy-p1-I2-1793142034/deliverables) and pass `lessons` as an after-action review: Expected / Happened / Caught at / Cause / Prevent (the system cause, not a person), or Near miss when nothing went wrong."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "## Budget plan"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "- [P7] Request budget: 12 runs (the contract's). Hand down no more than this up front, each with `budget=` set explicitly:"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "- [P8] writer: 3 runs (2 work + 1 rework or re-check)"
            }
          ],
